A||||10||Leadfoot||What a day!||||8||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||08-23-2001||11:08 AM||||What is with all this truck tire tread trash on the highways?!  Yesterday on my way back from school I hit one of those d@m things.  Almost broke my front end facia.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    I was passing a big a$$ explorer and right in the middle of the passing lane was a coiled up truck tire tread.  I tried to miss it but it was too late....Ca Clunk...Smack....Clatter....Thud.  The poor guy behind me hit it too and I saw that it lodged under his car.  We both pulled over and checked for damage.  Thank God there was none.  So I get back in my car and continue my drive.  About five miles from my exit the car stumbles and dies....now what?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> So I pulled over to the shoulder and tried to start it.  The car would start but quickly die.  I looked at the fuel gauge and guess what.....1/2 a tank.  I looked over at the od and it had 210 miles, which means NO GAS!  Usually my gauge would show just under a 1/4 tank before it went empty.  So I called my girlfriend on the cell phone to see if she can stop by and get some gas for me (nearest gas station was about 3 miles away and it was raining pretty hard outside).  She said she would be there in 45 minutes which was great.  As I was waiting a tow truck stops and asks what is the matter.  I told him I had no gas so he just turned around and got in his truck.  THANKS FOR NOTHING.  During the whole time I was waiting a total of 8 state troops passed me and not one of them stopped but you can bet your a$$ as soon as I left my car they would stop and put a nice bright orange tow warning on my window.  An hour passed an my girlfriend said she can't find me.  So I tell her my position again.  About five minutes later I see her car in the rear view mirror but don't see her pulling over.  I jump out of the car yelling and waving but she just past me by.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> She had to make another pass but saw me the second time around.  I then poured the gallon of gas she brought me in my car, started it up and took off for the nearest gas station.  I found a mobile gas station, pulled near a pump and filled her up.  As I pulled out of the station there was an expedition in front of me at the exit.  The guy decides at the last minute that he wants to take a different exit and starts to back up.  I start laying on the horn and by the time he realizes that I am behind him, his rear bumper is over my hood.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Luckly it didn't touch. After I yelled out a few choice words I backed up and went around him.  By the time I get home it was pouring cats and dogs.  I pull up to my driveway and prepared myself for a soaking experience.  Finally, I get into my house and as I am standing there drenched I see a box with my name on it sitting on the stairs. It was my subsystem that I bought from fleabitdog. IMG]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bounce.gif[/IMG] After seeing that box all of my ill tempered thoughts of destroying the world quickly subsided.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It's little pick me ups like these that make a great ending to an otherwise craptastic day.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Thank you for listening (reading).   <P>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-23-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Urchin||08-23-2001||12:07 PM||||Wow, talk about a rough day.  Sounds like you got pretty lucky a couple of times too.  No damage after a couple of close calls in poor weather.  Have fun installing the sub.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_3.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||08-23-2001||01:18 PM||||Those truck tire treads are really bad news for me.  I have to keep an eye out constantly for those, other trash, and small boxes of kittens in the road since my bumper is only a few inches from the pavement.<P>One of our neighbors was coming back from a trip from Montana pulling a 5th wheel behind their GMC 2500 pickup.  Just a few miles from home on the highway one of those treads jumped up from the car ahead and it took out the transmission lines on their truck.<P>That's gotta suck, make sure the tread didn't catch on anything under your car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000003||Formula88||08-23-2001||01:26 PM||||MAN, what a GREAT day you had!  Really.  To have gone through all that and you and your car come out unscathed?  Yeah, you were lucky!  <P>"I used to think I wasn't lucky, but then I realized, I didn't know what <I>hadn't</I> happened to me!"<P>------------------<BR>"God made us brothers.  Prozac made us friends." :D||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||08-23-2001||01:51 PM||||The CB'ers call them road gators. I smacked one of them at night at 70 mph going across I-80 in PA, caught me right in the front license plate. Put spider cracks all over the front bumper cover. (This was on the way to the photo shoot for Hot Rod too)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||08-24-2001||01:25 AM||||My saga continues.  Today I was driving to work and as I rolled down the window I smelled a strong odor of gas.  Thinking that it was the plastic tank that I placed in my trunk yesterday, I pulled over in a little mall parking lot to investigate.  I opened the deck lid and looked at the tank....it wasn't leaking.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  I quickly dropped to the ground and looked for any wet spots.  Sure enough there was a steady drip coming from the engine compartment.  It was coming from the cold start injector tube assembly right at the connection to the fuel rail.  I quickly shut off the engine and looked for a hardware store to see if I could by a cresent wrench to tighten the nut.  Luckly there was a true value in the mini-mall.  To make a long story short I wound up buying some gas tank patch epoxy to suppress the leak.  I drove home and took everything apart and found that the o-ring was torn.  Right now I am in the process of finding the correct o-ring.  So far I've been to several auto shops and the way it looks I might have to go to the dealer since no one carries such an o-ring of that size.  Snarbles!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-24-2001||11:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leadfoot:<BR><B>My saga continues.  Today I was driving to work and as I rolled down the window I smelled a strong odor of gas...  Sure enough there was a steady drip coming from the engine compartment.  It was coming from the cold start injector tube assembly right at the connection to the fuel rail.  I quickly shut off the engine... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah. It's a pain in the @ss. But look at it this way... If you hadn't smelled the gas, your Fiero could have become a statistic. And given the weenies on the Probe board something to talk about. <P>Dodged another bullet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||08-24-2001||12:18 PM||||That's why I suggested you to check everything again because I wondered if running out of gas had something to do with the tire tread.<P>Glad you found it and no fire!||||reg||4
Z||000008||Galen||08-24-2001||12:37 PM||||Dear Fiero Gods, shall all this mans fiero woes be solved quickly and cheaply.. for our brother needs help. Save this man from travelling to who knows how many stores to find this lil O-ring.. Fiero Gods! We Pray To Thee<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cooter||08-24-2001||08:08 PM||||I hit one with my Civic on the way back from Kentucky and ripped the front air dam off the bumper (the factory one, I am not a ricer!). The impact was so much that the car left the ground, my feet hit the underside of the dash and it made a huge hump in the driver's side floor pan. It was a miracle that it did not catch on the front cross member and rip the radiator support out of the car. Count your blessings like I did, it could have been much worse.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Leadfoot||08-24-2001||10:20 PM||||Thanks for caring everyone. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Just to give you an update, I finally went to the dealer and ordered the cold start injector gasket kit.  The dealership doesn't sell just the o-ring.  The kit is $15 and I'll post the part number when it comes in.  It might be of use to people rebuilding their engines.  Til then I guess I have to drive my jeep.  Boy it's been a long time since I drove it.  It's almost as fun as the fiero minus the get up and go.||||reg||1
